  - id: O:chart/foundation
    type: chart
    name: The Foundation's structure
    summary: A Board of Trustees, one Chief Executive Officer, seven departments; 685 staff on 2025-12-31 (the annual plan also says over 640).
    root: O:position/board-of-trustees
    headcount: {staff: 685, as-of: 2025-12-31, growth-12-months: "4.21%"}
    status: active
    visibility: public
    owner: O:role/chief-people-officer
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation_Annual_Plan/2026-2027/Budget_Overview", "https://wikimediafoundation.org/role/staff/"], confidence: 0.8, state: known}
    pending: "who reports to whom, and the executive team's decision rights: the public pages list titles and departments, not reporting lines"

  - id: O:decision-right/bylaws-and-policies
    type: decision-right
    name: Appointing the Chief Executive Officer
    summary: The Board appoints the Chief Executive Officer, a non-Trustee officer, and the Secretary and the Treasurer.
    holder: O:role/board-of-trustees
    over: O:position/chief-executive-officer
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Bylaws"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: O:decision-right/reserve
    type: decision-right
    name: Setting the reserve
    summary: The Board sets by resolution the minimum (12 months) and target (up to 18 months) of working capital.
    holder: O:role/board-of-trustees
    over: C:policy/reserves
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation_reports/Financial/Audits/2024-2025_-_frequently_asked_questions", "https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation_Annual_Plan/2026-2027/Budget_Overview"], confidence: 0.85, state: known}

  - id: O:decision-right/affiliation-models
    type: decision-right
    name: Recognising affiliation models
    summary: The Board recognises chapters, thematic organizations and user groups as affiliation models (approved 2012-03-31); the Affiliations Committee advises on each recognition.
    holder: O:role/board-of-trustees
    over: M:audience/affiliates
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_movement_affiliates"], confidence: 0.85, state: known}

  - id: O:decision-right/conduct
    type: decision-right
    name: Approving the Universal Code of Conduct
    summary: The Board approved the Universal Code of Conduct by resolution; sanctions are imposed by functionaries, the Foundation or both.
    holder: O:role/board-of-trustees
    over: C:policy/universal-code-of-conduct
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Universal_Code_of_Conduct"], confidence: 0.8, state: known}
